(5911031, 858929, 68769, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/>Hello Gerry, Im Alan.<br/> <br/>With a 6th place and a 6+ score I think you found a connection with the majority of the voters, that I personally found to be a creative take on a somewhat boring challenge. Your childs facial expression is perfect as well as the sky. Improvements? Except for the sky the colors look a tiny bit flat. I also feel your wife is but a minor distraction, explaining her in the title was unnecessary, a more creative title might have bumped the score a tiny amount. One other thing I would have done is apply a bit of Topaz Detail (disclaimer; Some topaz products are legal some questioned in basic, please check with SC with anything you do with this product) Free trial on the Topaz website (No, I do not have any association with Topaz).<br/>All in all, had I voted I would had rated a 8..<br/> <br/>If you have any questions on my insights please feel free to PM me.<br/>Alan.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.Hello Gerry, Im Alan. With a 6th place and a 6+ score I think you found a connection with the majority of the voters, that I personally found to be a creative take on a somewhat boring challenge. Your childs facial expression is perfect as well as the sky. Improvements? Except for the sky the colors look a tiny bit flat. I also feel your wife is but a minor distraction, explaining her in the title was unnecessary, a more creative title might have bumped the score a tiny amount. One other thing I would have done is apply a bit of Topaz Detail (disclaimer; Some topaz products are legal some questioned in basic, please check with SC with anything you do with this product) Free trial on the Topaz website (No, I do not have any association with Topaz).All in all, had I voted I would had rated a 8.. If you have any questions on my insights please feel free to PM me.Alan.', '2010-03-20 11:22:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5912279, 859528, 13688, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised of those who commented, no one really got the same reaction as me.  The feeling of distrust is extremely intense in this photo for me, because of the eyes.  Most are shifted, one is half closed, one has a scowl, and the front gentleman, who is clinging to his, most likely, only cherished possession, has a ''what you talkin'' bout Wilis'' look, but not in the cute, fuzzy way. That paired with the horrific poverty and the slap in the face of the consumerism, that is my world, with the gap logo, makes for an incredibly painful shot...almost like a car crash.  Thing is, I can''t figure out for sure if that was or wasn''t your intention.  I suppose I need to look through more of your work.  Thanks.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-21 22:54:47.</i></td>', 'I''m surprised of those who commented, no one really got the same reaction as me.  The feeling of distrust is extremely intense in this photo for me, because of the eyes.  Most are shifted, one is half closed, one has a scowl, and the front gentleman, who is clinging to his, most likely, only cherished possession, has a ''what you talkin'' bout Wilis'' look, but not in the cute, fuzzy way. That paired with the horrific poverty and the slap in the face of the consumerism, that is my world, with the gap logo, makes for an incredibly painful shot...almost like a car crash.  Thing is, I can''t figure out for sure if that was or wasn''t your intention.  I suppose I need to look through more of your work.  Thanks.', '2010-03-21 22:49:40.000000', '2010-03-21 22:54:47.000000', 0),
(5913147, 859069, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - before I read your comments, my first thought was "eerie!" so you definitely achieved your goal.  Very effective!</td>', 'Heh - before I read your comments, my first thought was "eerie!" so you definitely achieved your goal.  Very effective!', '2010-03-22 11:08:03.000000', NULL, 0),
