(5913938, 859552, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the DQ.  That''s what you get for trying to be me, you know...  :-)  (You''re a better photog than me, so I''m honored by the comparison!)</td>', 'Sorry about the DQ.  That''s what you get for trying to be me, you know...  :-)  (You''re a better photog than me, so I''m honored by the comparison!)', '2010-03-23 00:06:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5913980, 858748, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>First Impression: </b> When I first saw this picture I thought it fit the challenge well but might be a little out of focus.<br/> <br/><b>Composition: </b> The only thing I would change in terms of composition is to take a little space off the top, the background near the top is a little distracting. Little Miss Muffet is placed good and is sitting straight. It looks like it may have been taken on your bed and it looks like it has resulted in the bottle tilting slightly to the right.<br/> <br/><b>Subject: </b> Fits the challenge perfectly, a baby doll''s bottle and Miss Muffet are both children''s toys but are not related.<br/> <br/><b>Technical: </b> As mentioned in your comments your picture would have benefited from some contrast. It seems soft as well but that may be a personal choice. It gives a childhood dream quality to it.<br/> <br/><b>Final thoughts: </b> Ahhh you got beat up pretty hard by voters but don''t let that get you down. Best of luck in future challenges!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  First Impression:  When I first saw this picture I thought it fit the challenge well but might be a little out of focus. Composition:  The only thing I would change in terms of composition is to take a little space off the top, the background near the top is a little distracting. Little Miss Muffet is placed good and is sitting straight. It looks like it may have been taken on your bed and it looks like it has resulted in the bottle tilting slightly to the right. Subject:  Fits the challenge perfectly, a baby doll''s bottle and Miss Muffet are both children''s toys but are not related. Technical:  As mentioned in your comments your picture would have benefited from some contrast. It seems soft as well but that may be a personal choice. It gives a childhood dream quality to it. Final thoughts:  Ahhh you got beat up pretty hard by voters but don''t let that get you down. Best of luck in future challenges! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-03-23 01:54:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5913987, 859624, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>At first I thought it was part of the statue but that didn''t make any sense for the challenge. I think the only reason you didn''t score better with this picture is because the rabbit statues seem to be the main focal point.<br/> <br/>The focus looks great, maybe a wider aperture could have been used to put the rest of the picture out of focus leaving the duck sharp. Also a wee bit of contrast added would be nice.<br/> <br/>Overall I think this is a very strong image on a personal level, after reading your notes it makes more sense and shows the sentimental value that the voters would not have known of. I wonder if you got any strange looks carrying around this duck :P<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   At first I thought it was part of the statue but that didn''t make any sense for the challenge. I think the only reason you didn''t score better with this picture is because the rabbit statues seem to be the main focal point. The focus looks great, maybe a wider aperture could have been used to put the rest of the picture out of focus leaving the duck sharp. Also a wee bit of contrast added would be nice. Overall I think this is a very strong image on a personal level, after reading your notes it makes more sense and shows the sentimental value that the voters would not have known of. I wonder if you got any strange looks carrying around this duck :P If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-03-23 02:06:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5914129, 859618, 54885, '<td valign="top">Excellent image! Well deserved first place-this seems so simple but says so much</td>', 'Excellent image! Well deserved first place-this seems so simple but says so much', '2010-03-23 08:45:50.000000', NULL, 0),
